# .gitignore file for a Django project

This `.gitignore` file is a comprehensive list of common files and directories to exclude from version control in a Django project. It's designed to keep your repository clean of temporary files, security credentials, and environment-specific data.

-----

## Recommended `.gitignore` File

```
# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# C extensions
*.so

# Distribution / packaging
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
eggs/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

# Installer logs
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt

# Unit test / coverage reports
.coverage
.tox/
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage.*


.env
# virtualenv
.env
.venv
venv/
env/
/bin/
/include/
/lib/
/lib64/
/share/

# Django-specific files
*.log
*.pot
*.mo
*.prof

# Django security & media files
/media/
/static/
db.sqlite3
/local_settings.py

# Editor files
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Mac OS X folder attributes
.Trashes
```